item('RETRO-06',['00446','00449'],'Dose-level reductions were interpreted from standard level 0, ignoring actual prior component dose; 00449 had no current-level inputs.','Mapped every level change to current component level; added 00449 dose-history inputs. Missing history produces current-level-required output; cumulative level −3 produces discontinue.',{'00446':'p3 table1; p4 table2; p6 tables5–6','00449':'p3 table1; p4 table2; p6 table6'})
item('RETRO-07',['00446','00449'],'Nadir/toxicity rules could select a restart dose with unknown delay duration; 00449 GI highest grades triggered without current recovery and haematological reduction checked only one count.','Restart dose selection requires both counts where relevant, recovery grade and source-specific four-week (00446) or two-week (00449) window. Added missing-context and late-recovery review.',{'00446':'p4 table2; p6 table6','00449':'p4 table2; p6 table6'})
item('RETRO-08',['00446','00449'],'Source initial fluorouracil hepatic percentages could reset subsequent treatment to a fraction of the original dose, regardless of prior reductions.','Restricted numeric initial hepatic fractions to baseline assessment. Subsequent or unknown phase requires consultant review of actual prior dose and current toxicity.',{'00446':'p4 table3','00449':'p4 table3'})
item('RETRO-09',['00446','00449'],'Only uncontrolled/symptomatic hypertension hold existed; grade4 or persisting grade3 permanent stop was absent.','Added explicit clinically assessed grade4/persisting-grade3 bevacizumab discontinuation, tested with concurrent ordinary hypertension hold.',{'00446':'p5 table5','00449':'p5 table5'})
item('RETRO-10',['00446','00449'],'Arterial-event rule did not cover all source grade4 thromboembolic events, including life-threatening venous events.','Added separate grade4 thromboembolism bevacizumab stop, without applying it to all lower-grade venous events.',{'00446':'p5 table5; p7 venous-thromboembolism narrative','00449':'p5 table5; p7 venous-thromboembolism narrative'})
item('RETRO-11',['00448'],'Recovered counts after two weeks had no explicit source-window review. Febrile-neutropenia dose reduction could still print a numeric dose after late recovery.','Added late-count-recovery review; applied two-week recovery gate and missing-recovery review to the febrile-neutropenia restart branch.',{'00448':'p4 table2'})
item('RETRO-12',['00448'],'Unknown or late GI recovery suppressed numeric restart rules but did not explicitly explain the missing/late recovery decision.','Added explicit diarrhoea and stomatitis recovery-context reviews. Retained the separate requirement for full resolution of irinotecan-related diarrhoea.',{'00448':'p5 table4; p3 dose-modification recovery narrative'},'moderate')
item('RETRO-13',['00448'],'Coverage register still recorded source 4b while current protocol metadata and retrieved source are version5.','Current PDF v5/hash confirmed; stable protocol/canonical identifiers intentionally retained. Shared coverage correction handed to root owner.',{'00448':'PDF header/footer pp1–10; current HSE GI catalogue'},'moderate','handoff_shared_register')
